From 76b2d7e894a3da1bcb293845578ab98583196e0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nectura <45967738+Nectura@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:28:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): never dial a runtime stand-in's port -1 as the
 editor

A playtest started with no editor open self-heals a runtime-only
registry entry with "port": -1. The bridge took that port unchecked:

- at startup, portConfig resolved editor=-1 and createBridge crashed
  with ERR_INVALID_URL (ws://127.0.0.1:-1) before the MCP handshake;
- mid-session, rediscoverEditor adopted -1 after a connection loss,
  and every later call failed with "Invalid URL". That error is not a
  BridgeError, so the registry was never read again and the session
  stayed stuck until the client reconnected.

Every editor-port reader now goes through editorPortOf(), which only
accepts an integer 1-65535: startup falls back to the default port,
re-discovery skips the entry, and the pinned desync check reports it
as no live editor.

Unpinned re-discovery now also runs on AUTH_FAILED. A server that
started on the default port while only a stand-in was registered can
reach a different project's editor there; its auth then fails on every
call and, with no connection loss, the editor this project opens later
on another port was never found. When the registry agrees with the
cached port nothing swaps and the original error propagates, so a real
token problem still surfaces unchanged.
